/**
 * Search users whose `name` or `email` matches a free-text query string.
 *
 * The match is case-insensitive (ILIKE) and substring-based (wrapped in %).
 * The search term is always a bind parameter — never interpolated — so
 * SQL injection is impossible regardless of what the caller passes.
 *
 * @param {string} query          - Search term (must be non-empty)
 * @param {number} [limit]        - Rows per page
 * @param {number} [offset=0]     - Rows to skip
 * @returns {Promise<{ users: object[], total: number, limit: number, offset: number, query: string }>}
 *
